56
00:02:44,185 --> 00:02:47,063
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

57
00:02:47,290 --> 00:02:51,340
Step one: review personnel and
unit location age settings.

58
00:02:51,589 --> 00:02:55,512
Step two: add stations and
hospitals as points of interest.

59
00:02:55,735 --> 00:02:59,975
Step three: add a relevant map
layer, planned route, or weather

60
00:02:59,975 --> 00:03:01,713
zone, and review its audience.

61
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:04,164
Now verify the result.

62
00:03:04,382 --> 00:03:09,323
Check marker age and source, POI
placement, reference layer alignment,

63
00:03:09,475 --> 00:03:11,509
and the intended weather alert coverage.

64
00:03:11,704 --> 00:03:16,780
A common problem to watch for: location
sharing requires client permission.

65
00:03:16,987 --> 00:03:19,743
Uploaded floor plans
are reference material.

66
00:03:19,912 --> 00:03:23,266
Verify currency and alignment
before relying on them.

67
00:03:24,067 --> 00:03:25,897
Your practice task is simple.

68
00:03:26,114 --> 00:03:30,491
Follow a sample unit and compare a
recent position with a stale position.

69
00:03:30,687 --> 00:03:33,968
Record missing POIs and
outdated reference layers.

70
00:03:34,171 --> 00:03:38,682
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

71
00:03:38,824 --> 00:03:42,766
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
